[2026-03-14T19:39:43.583Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017trmuQxWy6iVqiHWwv7frS","type":"tool_result","content":"  1000→- **Action:** User clicks \"WiFi\" to uncheck it, then checks it again.\n  1001→- **Expected:** The checkbox toggles correctly on each click.\n  1002→\n  1003→#### Test: Step 5 — Photo URL input displayed\n  1004→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 4 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1005→- **Expected:** Step 5 is displayed with an input field for image URLs and an \"Add Photo\" button. A list/grid of added photos is shown below (initially empty). The step indicator shows Step 5 of 7.\n  1006→\n  1007→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding a photo URL\n  1008→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5.\n  1009→- **Action:** User types \"https://example.com/photo1.jpg\" in the URL input and clicks \"Add Photo\".\n  1010→- **Expected:** The photo URL is added to the list. A preview or thumbnail of the image is displayed. The URL input is cleared for the next entry. An optional caption field may be shown for the added photo.\n  1011→\n  1012→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding multiple photo URLs\n  1013→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with one photo already added.\n  1014→- **Action:** User adds two more photo URLs.\n  1015→- **Expected:** All three photos are displayed in the list/grid. Each photo can be reordered or removed.\n  1016→\n  1017→#### Test: Step 5 — Removing a photo\n  1018→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with 3 photos added.\n  1019→- **Action:** User clicks the remove/delete button on the second photo.\n  1020→- **Expected:** The second photo is removed from the list. The remaining 2 photos are displayed.\n  1021→\n  1022→#### Test: Step 5 — Validation requires at least one photo\n  1023→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with no photos added.\n  1024→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1025→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"At least one photo is required\"). The form does not advance.\n  1026→\n  1027→#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n  1028→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1029→- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n  1030→\n  1031→#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n  1032→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n  1033→- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n  1034→- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n  1035→\n  1036→#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n  1037→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n  1038→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1039→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n  1040→\n  1041→#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n  1042→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1043→- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n  1044→\n  1045→#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n  1046→- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75.\n  1047→- **Expected:** The review page displays all of these values accurately. No data is missing or incorrect.\n  1048→\n  1049→#### Test: Publishing a new listing creates the property\n  1050→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 7 (Review) with all data entered correctly.\n  1051→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Publish\" button.\n  1052→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/properties` with the property data, then `POST /api/property-images` for each photo. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing published successfully!\"). The form closes. The new property appears in the Listings tab grid. The \"Total Listings\" stat increments by 1.\n  1053→\n  1054→#### Test: Back button navigates to the previous step\n  1055→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 3 of the Add Listing form.\n  1056→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Back\" button.\n  1057→- **Expected:** The form navigates to Step 2. All previously entered data in Step 2 is preserved (city, address, etc. are still filled).\n  1058→\n  1059→#### Test: Cancel button closes the form without saving\n  1060→- **Initial state:** User is on Step 4 of the Add Listing form with data entered in Steps 1–3.\n  1061→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button.\n  1062→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Discard your listing? All entered information will be lost.\" with \"Discard\" and \"Keep Editing\" buttons.\n  1063→\n  1064→#### Test: Confirming cancel discards the listing form\n  1065→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1066→- **Action:** User clicks \"Discard\".\n  1067→- **Expected:** The form closes. No API calls are made. The user returns to the Listings tab. No new property is created.\n  1068→\n  1069→#### Test: Dismissing cancel keeps the form open\n  1070→- **Initial state:** The discard confirmation dialog is open.\n  1071→- **Action:** User clicks \"Keep Editing\".\n  1072→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The form remains on the current step with all data preserved.\n  1073→\n  1074→#### Test: Step indicator shows correct progress throughout the form\n  1075→- **Initial state:** User opens the Add Listing form.\n  1076→- **Action:** User navigates through all 7 steps using Next/Back buttons.\n  1077→- **Expected:** The step indicator accurately shows the current step (e.g., \"Step 1 of 7\", \"Step 2 of 7\", etc.) at each stage. Completed steps may show a checkmark or different styling.\n  1078→\n  1079→#### Test: Data persistence across steps when navigating back and forth\n  1080→- **Initial state:** User has filled out Steps 1–5 and is on Step 5.\n  1081→- **Action:** User clicks \"Back\" twice to Step 3, then \"Next\" twice to Step 5.\n  1082→- **Expected:** All data entered in Steps 3, 4, and 5 is preserved after navigating back and forth. No data is lost.\n  1083→\n  1084→#### Test: Add Listing form works correctly on repeated use\n  1085→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. User has already published one listing successfully.\n  1086→- **Action:** User clicks \"Add Listing\" again, fills out all steps, and publishes.\n  1087→- **Expected:** A second property is created successfully. Both properties appear in the Listings tab. The \"Total Listings\" stat shows the correct total.\n  1088→\n  1089→## Page: User Profile (`/profile`)\n  1090→\n  1091→<!-- Components: ProfileForm, BecomeHostButton, UserReviewsList -->\n  1092→\n  1093→### Component: ProfileForm\n  1094→\n  1095→#### Test: Profile page requires login\n  1096→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n  1097→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1098→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to `/login`. The profile page is not displayed.\n  1099→\n  1100→#### Test: Profile page displays current user info\n  1101→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\", bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\".\n  1102→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1103→- **Expected:** The profile form displays the current values: name \"Alice Smith\", email \"alice@example.com\" (read-only), bio \"Love traveling!\", phone \"555-1234\", and avatar URL \"https://example.com/avatar.jpg\". The avatar image is displayed using the URL.\n  1104→\n  1105→#### Test: Edit name field inline\n  1106→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1107→- **Action:** User clicks the name field, clears it, types \"Alice Johnson\", and clicks the \"Save\" button.\n  1108→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated name. The name field displays \"Alice Johnson\". A success message (e.g., \"Profile updated\") is shown. The Redux user state is updated with the new name.\n  1109→\n  1110→#### Test: Edit bio field inline\n  1111→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Love traveling!\".\n  1112→- **Action:** User clicks the bio textarea, clears it, types \"Digital nomad and foodie\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1113→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated bio. The bio field displays \"Digital nomad and foodie\". A success message is shown.\n  1114→\n  1115→#### Test: Edit phone field inline\n  1116→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with phone \"555-1234\".\n  1117→- **Action:** User clicks the phone field, clears it, types \"555-9876\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1118→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated phone. The phone field displays \"555-9876\". A success message is shown.\n  1119→\n  1120→#### Test: Edit avatar URL field inline\n  1121→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with avatar URL \"https://example.com/old-avatar.jpg\".\n  1122→- **Action:** User clicks the avatar URL field, clears it, types \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\", and clicks \"Save\".\n  1123→- **Expected:** A `PUT /api/users/:id` request is sent with the updated avatar URL. The avatar image preview updates to show the new image from \"https://example.com/new-avatar.jpg\". A success message is shown.\n  1124→\n  1125→#### Test: Save with empty name shows validation error\n  1126→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1127→- **Action:** User clears the name field (leaving it empty) and clicks \"Save\".\n  1128→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made. The name field is highlighted as invalid.\n  1129→\n  1130→#### Test: Save with invalid avatar URL shows validation error\n  1131→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile`.\n  1132→- **Action:** User enters \"not-a-url\" in the avatar URL field and clicks \"Save\".\n  1133→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid URL\"). No API call is made.\n  1134→\n  1135→#### Test: Profile form fields are functional on repeated edits\n  1136→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with name \"Alice Smith\".\n  1137→- **Action:** User changes the name to \"Alice Johnson\" and clicks \"Save\". After the success message, user changes the name again to \"Alice Williams\" and clicks \"Save\".\n  1138→- **Expected:** Both saves succeed with separate `PUT /api/users/:id` requests. After the second save, the name field displays \"Alice Williams\". Both updates are persisted.\n  1139→\n  1140→#### Test: Email field is displayed but not editable\n  1141→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with email \"alice@example.com\".\n  1142→- **Action:** User views the profile form.\n  1143→- **Expected:** The email \"alice@example.com\" is displayed but the field is read-only / disabled and cannot be edited.\n  1144→\n  1145→#### Test: Profile update persists across navigation\n  1146→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on `/profile` with bio \"Old bio\".\n  1147→- **Action:** User changes bio to \"New bio\", clicks \"Save\", then navigates to `/` (home page), then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1148→- **Expected:** The bio field displays \"New bio\", confirming the change was persisted to the database and Redux state.\n  1149→\n  1150→### Component: BecomeHostButton\n  1151→\n  1152→#### Test: Become a Host button is visible for non-host users\n  1153→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false`.\n  1154→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1155→- **Expected:** A \"Become a Host\" button is visible on the profile page.\n  1156→\n  1157→#### Test: Become a Host button is hidden for existing hosts\n  1158→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `true`.\n  1159→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1160→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is NOT visible on the profile page.\n  1161→\n  1162→#### Test: Clicking Become a Host sets user as host\n  1163→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1164→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button.\n  1165→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears (e.g., \"Are you sure you want to become a host?\"). User confirms. A `POST /api/users/:id/become-host` request is sent. Upon success, the button disappears, a success message is shown (e.g., \"You are now a host!\"), and the Redux user state updates `is_host` to `true`. The \"Hosting\" link becomes available in the navigation sidebar.\n  1166→\n  1167→#### Test: Cancel Become a Host confirmation dialog\n  1168→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`. The \"Become a Host\" button is visible.\n  1169→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Become a Host\" button, then clicks \"Cancel\" in the confirmation dialog.\n  1170→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. No API call is made. The \"Become a Host\" button remains visible. `is_host` remains `false`.\n  1171→\n  1172→#### Test: Become a Host button appearance\n  1173→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with `is_host` set to `false` and on `/profile`.\n  1174→- **Action:** User views the profile page.\n  1175→- **Expected:** The \"Become a Host\" button is styled with the coral/red accent color (#FF5A5F), has clear text reading \"Become a Host\", and is visually prominent on the page.\n  1176→\n  1177→### Component: UserReviewsList\n  1178→\n  1179→#### Test: Reviews list displays user's written reviews\n  1180→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written 3 reviews for different properties (e.g., \"Cozy Cabin\" rated 5, \"City Apartment\" rated 3, \"Beach Villa\" rated 4).\n  1181→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1182→- **Expected:** A \"My Reviews\" section is visible showing all 3 reviews. Each review card displays: the property title, the overall rating (with filled/unfilled stars), the comment text, and the date the review was written.\n  1183→\n  1184→#### Test: Reviews list shows empty state for user with no reviews\n  1185→- **Initial state:** User is logged in but has not written any reviews.\n  1186→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1187→- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You haven't written any reviews yet\") instead of review cards.\n  1188→\n  1189→#### Test: Review card shows rating with star display\n  1190→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with overall rating 4 out of 5.\n  1191→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1192→- **Expected:** The review card displays 4 filled stars and 1 unfilled star, matching the rating value.\n  1193→\n  1194→#### Test: Review card links to the reviewed property\n  1195→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review for property \"Cozy Cabin\" (property ID \"abc-123\").\n  1196→- **Action:** User clicks on the property title \"Cozy Cabin\" in a review card.\n  1197→- **Expected:** The user is navigated to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page for \"Cozy Cabin\").\n  1198→\n  1199→#### Test: Reviews list shows review details correctly\n  1200→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written a review with rating 5, comment \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", for property \"Beach Villa\", dated \"2026-01-15\".\n  1201→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1202→- **Expected:** The review card displays: property title \"Beach Villa\", 5 filled stars, comment text \"Amazing stay! The host was very welcoming.\", and date \"Jan 15, 2026\".\n  1203→\n  1204→#### Test: Reviews list updates after writing a new review\n  1205→- **Initial state:** User is logged in, on `/profile`, and has 2 existing reviews displayed.\n  1206→- **Action:** User navigates to a completed booking, writes a new review, submits it, then navigates back to `/profile`.\n  1207→- **Expected:** The \"My Reviews\" section now displays 3 reviews, including the newly written review with the correct property title, rating, and comment.\n  1208→\n  1209→#### Test: Reviews list shows multiple reviews in chronological order\n  1210→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has written reviews on different dates: \"Beach Villa\" on 2026-01-15, \"City Apartment\" on 2026-02-10, \"Cozy Cabin\" on 2026-03-05.\n  1211→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1212→- **Expected:** The reviews are displayed in reverse chronological order (newest first): \"Cozy Cabin\" (Mar 5, 2026), \"City Apartment\" (Feb 10, 2026), \"Beach Villa\" (Jan 15, 2026).\n  1213→\n  1214→## Page: Write Review (`/trips/:bookingId/review`)\n  1215→\n  1216→<!-- Components: ReviewForm, RatingSliders, PropertyBookingContext -->\n  1217→\n  1218→### Component: PropertyBookingContext\n  1219→\n  1220→#### Test: Property info displays for the booking being reviewed\n  1221→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in and has a completed booking (booking-789) for \"Oceanfront Villa\" in Malibu, CA with check-in 2026-01-10 and check-out 2026-01-15.\n  1222→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1223→- **Expected:** The page displays the property context section showing the property title \"Oceanfront Villa\", the location \"Malibu, CA\", the property's main image, check-in date \"Jan 10, 2026\", check-out date \"Jan 15, 2026\", and the number of nights (5 nights).\n  1224→\n  1225→#### Test: Property booking context shows guest count\n  1226→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) for 3 guests at \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n  1227→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1228→- **Expected:** The property booking context section displays \"3 guests\" alongside the booking dates.\n  1229→\n  1230→#### Test: Property booking context shows total price paid\n  1231→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with a completed booking (booking-789) with a total_price of $1,250.\n  1232→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1233→- **Expected:** The property booking context displays the total price \"$1,250\" that was paid for the booking.\n  1234→\n  1235→#### Test: Redirect to login if not authenticated\n  1236→- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n  1237→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1238→- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Write Review page is not displayed.\n  1239→\n  1240→#### Test: Error state when booking does not exist\n  1241→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in.\n  1242→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/nonexistent-booking-id/review`.\n  1243→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"Booking not found\" and does not show the review form.\n  1244→\n  1245→#### Test: Error state when booking belongs to another user\n  1246→- **Initial state:** User \"other@example.com\" is logged in. Booking booking-789 belongs to \"guest@example.com\".\n  1247→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review`.\n  1248→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You cannot review this booking\" and does not show the review form.\n  1249→\n  1250→#### Test: Error state when booking is not completed\n  1251→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a booking (booking-pending) that has status \"pending\".\n  1252→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-pending/review`.\n  1253→- **Expected:** The page displays an error message such as \"You can only review completed bookings\" and does not show the review form.\n  1254→\n  1255→#### Test: Error state when review already exists for booking\n  1256→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" is logged in with a completed booking (booking-reviewed) that already has a review submitted.\n  1257→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-reviewed/review`.\n  1258→- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" and does not show the review form. Optionally shows a link back to My Trips.\n  1259→\n  1260→### Component: RatingSliders\n  1261→\n  1262→#### Test: All six rating sliders display with default values\n  1263→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n  1264→- **Expected:** Six rating sliders are visible with labels: \"Overall\", \"Cleanliness\", \"Accuracy\", \"Communication\", \"Location\", and \"Value\". Each slider defaults to a mid-range value (e.g., 3 out of 5) or is unset, and shows the current numeric value.\n  1265→\n  1266→#### Test: Adjust overall rating slider\n  1267→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1268→- **Action:** User drags the \"Overall\" slider to 5.\n  1269→- **Expected:** The \"Overall\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display next to the slider updates to \"5\". Other sliders remain at their previous values.\n  1270→\n  1271→#### Test: Adjust cleanliness rating slider\n  1272→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1273→- **Action:** User drags the \"Cleanliness\" slider to 4.\n  1274→- **Expected:** The \"Cleanliness\" slider displays value 4. The numeric display updates to \"4\".\n  1275→\n  1276→#### Test: Adjust accuracy rating slider\n  1277→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1278→- **Action:** User drags the \"Accuracy\" slider to 2.\n  1279→- **Expected:** The \"Accuracy\" slider displays value 2. The numeric display updates to \"2\".\n  1280→\n  1281→#### Test: Adjust communication rating slider\n  1282→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1283→- **Action:** User drags the \"Communication\" slider to 5.\n  1284→- **Expected:** The \"Communication\" slider displays value 5. The numeric display updates to \"5\".\n  1285→\n  1286→#### Test: Adjust location rating slider\n  1287→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1288→- **Action:** User drags the \"Location\" slider to 3.\n  1289→- **Expected:** The \"Location\" slider displays value 3. The numeric display updates to \"3\".\n  1290→\n  1291→#### Test: Adjust value rating slider\n  1292→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1293→- **Action:** User drags the \"Value\" slider to 1.\n  1294→- **Expected:** The \"Value\" slider displays value 1. The numeric display updates to \"1\".\n  1295→\n  1296→#### Test: Rating sliders enforce 1-5 range\n  1297→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n  1298→- **Action:** User interacts with any rating slider.\n  1299→- **Expected:** The slider only allows integer values from 1 to 5 inclusive. The slider cannot go below 1 or above 5.\n  1300→\n  1301→#### Test: Multiple sliders can be set independently\n  1302→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with all sliders at default.\n  1303→- **Action:** User sets \"Overall\" to 5, \"Cleanliness\" to 4, \"Accuracy\" to 3, \"Communication\" to 5, \"Location\" to 4, \"Value\" to 2.\n  1304→- **Expected:** Each slider displays its independently set value. No slider affects another slider's value.\n  1305→\n  1306→#### Test: Rating slider visual feedback shows filled stars or highlighted segments\n  1307→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n  1308→- **Action:** User sets the \"Overall\" slider to 4.\n  1309→- **Expected:** The slider visually indicates the selected rating (e.g., filled stars up to 4 out of 5, or a highlighted slider track up to the 4 position). The visual feedback clearly distinguishes selected vs unselected portions.\n  1310→\n  1311→### Component: ReviewForm\n  1312→\n  1313→#### Test: Review form displays comment text area\n  1314→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` for a completed booking.\n  1315→- **Expected:** A text area is visible with a placeholder such as \"Write your review...\" or \"Tell others about your experience\" for entering the review comment.\n  1316→\n  1317→#### Test: Submit button is visible\n  1318→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n  1319→- **Expected:** A \"Submit Review\" button is visible at the bottom of the form.\n  1320→\n  1321→#### Test: Type a comment in the text area\n  1322→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page with an empty comment text area.\n  1323→- **Action:** User types \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\" in the comment text area.\n  1324→- **Expected:** The text area displays the typed text \"Amazing stay! The villa was beautiful and the host was very responsive.\"\n  1325→\n  1326→#### Test: Submit review with all ratings and comment\n  1327→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5, Cleanliness to 5, Accuracy to 4, Communication to 5, Location to 4, Value to 4, and typed \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\" in the comment area.\n  1328→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n  1329→- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully via `POST /api/reviews`. The app navigates back to `/trips` (My Trips page). A success notification or message such as \"Review submitted successfully\" appears.\n  1330→\n  1331→#### Test: Submitted review appears on property detail page\n  1332→- **Initial state:** User just submitted a review for booking-789 (property \"Oceanfront Villa\") with Overall rating 5 and comment \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\".\n  1333→- **Action:** User navigates to the property detail page for \"Oceanfront Villa\" (`/properties/:id`).\n  1334→- **Expected:** The reviews section shows the newly submitted review with the guest's name, the rating of 5, and the comment \"Wonderful experience, would definitely come back!\". The property's average rating and review count are updated.\n  1335→\n  1336→#### Test: Submitted review appears in user profile reviews list\n  1337→- **Initial state:** User just submitted a review for \"Oceanfront Villa\".\n  1338→- **Action:** User navigates to `/profile`.\n  1339→- **Expected:** The user's reviews list includes the newly submitted review for \"Oceanfront Villa\" with the correct rating and comment.\n  1340→\n  1341→#### Test: Submit review with ratings but no comment\n  1342→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set all six rating sliders (Overall: 3, Cleanliness: 3, Accuracy: 3, Communication: 3, Location: 3, Value: 3) but left the comment text area empty.\n  1343→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n  1344→- **Expected:** The review is submitted successfully (comment is optional per the data model). The app navigates back to `/trips`.\n  1345→\n  1346→#### Test: Submit button is disabled when ratings are not set\n  1347→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the Write Review page. No rating sliders have been adjusted from their unset/default state.\n  1348→- **Expected:** The \"Submit Review\" button is disabled or grayed out, preventing submission without ratings.\n  1349→\n  1350→#### Test: Form validation prevents submission without all ratings\n  1351→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page. User has set Overall to 5 but left other rating sliders unset.\n  1352→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Submit Review\" button.\n  1353→- **Expected:** The form shows a validation error indicating all ratings are required (e.g., \"Please rate all categories\"). The review is not submitted.\n  1354→\n  1355→#### Test: Write Review button on My Trips disappears after submitting review\n  1356→- **Initial state:** User has a completed booking for \"Oceanfront Villa\" showing a \"Write Review\" button on the My Trips page.\n  1357→- **Action:** User clicks \"Write Review\", fills out all ratings (all set to 4) and a comment \"Great stay!\", and clicks \"Submit Review\". User is redirected to `/trips`.\n  1358→- **Expected:** The trip card for \"Oceanfront Villa\" no longer shows the \"Write Review\" button. It may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark instead.\n  1359→\n  1360→#### Test: Navigate back from review page without submitting\n  1361→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page and has set some ratings and typed partial comment text.\n  1362→- **Action:** User clicks the browser back button or a \"Cancel\" / back navigation link on the page.\n  1363→- **Expected:** The user is taken back to `/trips`. No review is submitted. The \"Write Review\" button still appears on the trip card.\n  1364→\n  1365→#### Test: Comment text area allows multi-line input\n  1366→- **Initial state:** User is on the Write Review page.\n  1367→- **Action:** User types a multi-line comment: \"First line.\\nSecond line.\\nThird line.\" using Enter/Return key to create line breaks.\n  1368→- **Expected:** The text area displays the comment with line breaks preserved across all three lines.\n  1369→\n  1370→#### Test: Re-visiting review page after submission shows already-reviewed state\n  1371→- **Initial state:** User \"guest@example.com\" has already submitted a review for booking-789.\n  1372→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips/booking-789/review` directly via URL.\n  1373→- **Expected:** The page displays a message such as \"You have already reviewed this booking\" instead of the review form. A link to return to My Trips is available.\n  1374→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ku8J7eurhAtADnCzyj19gD","session_id":"e9cade60-94a4-4669-9ce9-af24d9b0f1dc","uuid":"d9be6eaa-e4df-497b-b14e-3c70a64e12e2"}
